    "reason": "The English lemma 'change' (noun) is a very broad and general term for any alteration or transformation. While '転変' (tenpen) does mean 'change' or 'vicissitude' as per JMdict, it carries a more specific nuance of significant, dramatic, or continuous changes, often implying the flux of things or the vicissitudes of life/history. It is not the most common or natural general equivalent for 'change' that a learner would expect. The term '変化' (henka) is a much more general and natural choice for 'change' (noun) in most contexts.",
